 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "A Nagata domain is Japanese",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be an integral domain which is a Nagata ring [def-weil-pbc-nagata-ring]. Then $S$ is N-2 [def-weil-pbc-japanese-domain] with respect to its fraction field.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/algebra.tex",
  "place": "Algebra, Proposition Tag 0334 (proposition-nagata-universally-japanese)"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-pbc-nagata-ring",
  "def-weil-pbc-japanese-domain"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The zero ideal of the domain is prime, so the Nagata hypothesis gives N-2 for S/(0). The canonical quotient isomorphism S/(0) -> S is injective and finite. The source is Noetherian by the same isomorphism and the Nagata hypothesis. Apply ascent of N-2 along a finite domain extension to obtain N-2 for S.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-pbc-nagata-ring",
    "def-weil-pbc-japanese-domain",
    "lem-weil-pbc-n2-ascends-finite-domain-extension"
   ],
